      "text": "The prime factorization of $400$ is $2^4 \\cdot 5^2$.\nThe positive divisors of $400$ are $1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 16, 20, 25, 40, 50, 80, 100, 200, 250, 400$.\nWe can list them as $2^0 \\cdot 5^0, 2^1 \\cdot 5^0, \\ldots, 2^4 \\cdot 5^2$.\nThe sum of the divisors is $$(1 + 2 + \\cdots + 2^4) \\cdot (1 + 5 + \\cdots + 5^2) = (2^5 - 1)(5^3 - 1) = 31 \\cdot 124 = 3914.$$\nThe prime factorization of $3914$ is $2 \\cdot 1957.$\nThere are two distinct prime factors.\nSo, the answer is $\\boxed{2}.$\n\nSolve the following mathematics problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}:\n\nWhat is the value of $x^5 - 5x$ when $x = 4$?\n\nSolution:\nSubstitute $x = 4$ into the expression $x^5 - 5x$ to get $4^5 - 5(4) = 4096 - 20 = \\boxed{4076}.$ The answer is: 4076",
